---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ToVerify from '../../components/ToVerify.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Mayor's Court"
  description="The Mayor's Court of the Village of Midvale handles minor traffic and ordinance violations under Ohio R.C. Chapter 1905."
  eyebrow="Government"
  intro="Minor traffic and ordinance violations are heard in Mayor's Court."
>
  <section class="prose-village max-w-prose">
    <h2>About the Court</h2>
    <p>
      The Mayor's Court of the Village of Midvale operates under the authority
      of Ohio Revised Code Chapter 1905. The Court has jurisdiction over minor
      traffic and ordinance violations occurring within the village limits.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Location:</strong> {site.address.street}, {site.address.city}, {site.address.state} {site.address.zip}
    </p>

    <ToVerify note="Court session schedule, citation payment process, and continuance request process pending verification with the Police Chief and Fiscal Officer." />

    <h2>If you received a citation</h2>
    <p>
      The citation you received will indicate a court date. You generally have
      three options:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pay the citation</strong> &mdash; instructions on the citation, or contact the village office during business hours.</li>
      <li><strong>Appear in court</strong> &mdash; arrive at Village Hall on the date and time printed on your citation.</li>
      <li><strong>Request a continuance</strong> &mdash; contact the village office in advance to request a new court date.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>More serious matters</h2>
    <p>
      Mayor's Court only handles minor offenses. More serious matters are
      transferred to the New Philadelphia Municipal Court. Defendants always
      have the right to have their case transferred to a court of record.
    </p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
